    "differences": [],
    "decisions": {},
    "unresolved": [],
    "complete": true,
    "independent_text": "As one who sits in the protection of the Most High and shelters in the shadow of the Almighty, I say to the Lord: My refuge and my fortress, my God in whom I trust. For He saves you from the snare of the fowler, from destructive plague. With His wing He covers you, you shelter under His wings, His faithfulness is shield and buckler. You shall not fear the terror of night, the arrow that flies by day, the plague that creeps in the dark, the pestilence that flares up at noon. Though a thousand fall at your side and ten thousand on your right, to you it will not approach. You need only look with your eyes and you will see the recompense of the wicked. For Thou, O Lord, art my trust — on high hast Thou placed Thy dwelling. No misfortune will befall you, no plague will come near your tent. For He will command His angels concerning you to guard you in all your ways. On hands will they bear you lest your foot be bruised by a stone. Though you tread on the lion and viper and trample on the whelp and the crocodile. For because he delighted in Me I delivered him; I shall raise him up because he acknowledged my Name. When he calls me, I will answer him, I am with him in distress, I save him and honour him. With length of days will I satisfy him and I will let him see my salvation."
  },
